Good luck; Acer seem to be absolutely terrible at communicating with the 
outside world, or at least end-users - I must have spent an hour of hold-time 
or more altogether just in calls that they cut off before I even spoke to 
someone.

And when I got through, they either stuck to "we can't help you with this, 
it's outside of our scope, bring your machine to a repair centre" or "we only 
support Windows".
In the end, it was easier for me to buy a phonecard and call their offices in 
Taiwan than it was speaking to the nearest call-centre (the UK), who 
basically sucked and promised me emails I never received, etc.

I don't think Acer will help.

